<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first proposal. Source sgo ba is preserved and paired with stained: the binding HGM entry explicitly attests stain/stained; raw corpus witnesses ILL:1920 and C16:793 retain SGO BA, with related SGO GZHI at GK:353/362. This evidence does not establish independent publication or ingestion history and does not justify a spelling correction. The second kun gzhi rnam shes owns the object of focuses on; GMR's subsequent repetition of foundation consciousness is supplied and unwrapped. gnas owns place, with stay left unwrapped as a distributed verbal expansion. The two nga'o occurrences own the two quoted me tokens. snyam constructions and gzhir gyur pa'i are omitted because their contributions are distributed through the English recast.</div>
